        "subheadline_text_size": "copy-l",
        "subheadline_text_no_decal": false,
        "subheadline_text_strong_accented": false,
        "text": "<p>Learn the qualifications, skills and career path to support clients with long-term health conditions safely and professionally. </p><p>Becoming a <a href=\"https://studyactive.co.uk/products/active-iq-level-3-online-diploma-in-supporting-clients-with-long-term-conditions\" title=\"https://studyactive.co.uk/products/active-iq-level-3-online-diploma-in-supporting-clients-with-long-term-conditions\">Long-Term Conditions Exercise Specialist</a> allows you to work with clients who need expert, safe and structured support to improve their health. From managing chronic illnesses like diabetes and cardiovascular disease to improving mobility and quality of life, this specialist role is in high demand across the UK. </p><p>In this guide, you’ll learn how to get qualified, what skills you need, and how to start a rewarding career supporting clients with long-term conditions. </p>",
